WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.150
There's nothing quite like a good shock at
the movies.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:07.529
And while everyone loves to see their heroes
live happily ever after, sometimes audiences

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:10.500
need a reminder that life isn't all sunshine
and roses.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.460
Here are a few movies where the villain actually
wins.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.320
The Star Wars universe is no stranger to a
villainous victory or two, with warring space

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.140
factions trading constant blows back and forth
across various conflicts.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.960
Rogue One and Revenge of the Sith certainly
end on some down notes, for example, but the

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.620
series' most iconic Dark Side victory came
in the middle chapter of the original trilogy.

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:34.580
Following the first film, which left off on
a Death Star-destroying high, The Empire Strikes

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.510
Back came crashing back down to reality when
it opened with the crushing defeat of the

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:39.760
rebel forces on Hoth.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.920
While the movie splinters at that point, with
various characters heading off to do their

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.120
own thing, the paths of the protagonists ultimately
lead back to Lando Calrissian's floating haven

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.000
of Cloud City.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.420
Unfortunately, when Darth Vader and his minions
show up in Calrissian's city, things quickly

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.100
go south for pretty much everyone.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.840
Han Solo is tortured and used as a test subject
for carbon freezing, leaving him in suspended

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:00.460
animation.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.000
Calrissian loses Cloud City to the Empire.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.000
Meanwhile, Luke is lured into a trap and confronted
with one cinema's greatest ever twists.

00:01:07.001 --> 00:01:11.300
Needless to say, there's no doubt that Empire's
final act is a home run for Vader and the

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.940
Empire from start to finish.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.200
The 2008 film Valkyrie is inspired by the
failed assassination attempt made against

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.590
Adolf Hitler in the summer of 1944 by a cabal
of German officers aiming to overthrow the

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:24.640
Nazi regime.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:29.479
Colonel Claus von Stauffenberg joins Major-General
Henning von Tresckow and a number of other

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:34.270
conspirators, who set up a plan to kill off
the dictator and use the Reserve Army to maintain

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:37.060
order and establish themselves as the new
government.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:41.620
From there, they plan to use their power to
negotiate favorable peace terms with the Allies,

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:44.240
who at that point are on the clear path to
victory.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.270
The film follows the story just as it actually
unfolded, with everything seeming to move

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.500
towards victory for von Stauffenberg and his
co-conspirators.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:55.460
In fact, the movie does it so well it almost
makes you forget that you already know what's

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.340
about to go down.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.340
But alas, Valkyrie is ruthlessly tethered
to reality.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:04.260
Initially, the assassination comes tantalizingly
close to success, with the planted explosives

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:07.860
going off successfully and Operation Valkyrie
being put into action.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.320
But before long, reports surface that Hitler
survived the explosion, and from there the

00:02:12.329 --> 00:02:13.730
whole plot collapses.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.590
The movie ends with Hitler still alive and
the film's heroes executed for treason, which

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:20.920
is about as bad as things possibly could have
gone.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:25.980
Over the years, Marvel comics have seen plenty
of tragic endings and grisly cliffhangers,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:29.740
but the MCU itself has tended to prefer the
good guys to come out on top.

00:02:29.909 --> 00:02:33.540
But this trend has recently begun to change,
having kicked off in earnest when Captain

00:02:33.549 --> 00:02:39.159
America: Civil War pitted the Avengers against
one another, leaving a host of angry, PTSD-ridden

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.360
superheroes behind in the process.

00:02:40.669 --> 00:02:44.980
This slide downhill only sped up with Thor:
Ragnarok, an otherwise fun movie that ended

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:49.000
with Asgard destroyed and a small handful
of survivors setting out in search of a new

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:49.500
home.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.640
But it was only during Avengers: Infinity
War that Marvel finally opened up a universe

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.439
in which the villains really can win.

00:02:55.439 --> 00:02:59.889
This colossal crossover event finds the heroes
struggling to rise up and defend the universe

00:02:59.889 --> 00:03:04.379
against Thanos and his cronies, only for the
Mad Titan to finally pull off his cataclysmic

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:07.820
finger snap and wipe out half the universe
in the process.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.860
"I am inevitable."

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.439
While much of Thanos' mad destruction was
undone in Avengers: Endgame, Infinity War

00:03:15.439 --> 00:03:20.189
was nonetheless so focused on Thanos and his
story that his victory during the film's closing

00:03:20.189 --> 00:03:22.560
moments was never anything but inevitable.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.559
Se7en follows detectives William Somerset
and David Mills as they investigate a series

00:03:28.559 --> 00:03:33.120
of murders by a mysterious criminal who uses
the seven deadly sins as his calling card.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.379
The movie gains speed as the duo uncover the
first five sins, but before the last two take

00:03:37.379 --> 00:03:41.720
place, the murderer, known as John Doe, turns
himself in to the authorities while covered

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.200
in the blood of an unknown victim.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.699
As the movie wraps up, the growing sense of
impending doom becomes practically unbearable.

00:03:47.699 --> 00:03:51.890
Doe directs Mills and Somerset to the desert,
where he informs them that the last two victims

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:52.480
will be found.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.980
Of course, they're already present, as Doe
confesses to being envious of Mills' idyllic

00:03:56.989 --> 00:04:01.590
life with his pregnant wife Tracy before a
box arrives on the scene, containing Tracy's

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:02.460
head inside.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:07.040
Mills then gives in to temptation and kills
Doe, who becomes the final victim of wrath.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.199
Aside from being messed up in so many ways,
Se7en's plot is never in the hands of the

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:15.200
movie's protagonists, with Doe in total control
right up until the credits roll.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.480
Christopher Nolan's The Dark Knight delivered
more than just an outstanding performance

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:24.419
from a greatly-missed actor since Heath Ledger's
Joker was also one of the first superhero

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.120
villains to have his way with the hero from
beginning to end.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.940
From the moment he enters that dramatic opening
heist sequence to his last laugh during the

00:04:30.949 --> 00:04:34.669
film's climax, the infamous DC villain easily
steals the show.

00:04:34.669 --> 00:04:39.110
The Dark Knight revolves almost entirely around
the Joker's schemes against Gotham and Batman

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:40.920
many of which are pulled off without a hitch.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:45.920
As a result, this second film in Nolan's epic
trilogy leaves Rachel Dawes dead, Harvey Dent

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:50.550
warped into Two-Face and killed soon after,
Batman on the run after taking responsibility

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:54.069
for Dent's crimes, and the Bat-signal destroyed
by Commissioner Gordon.

00:04:54.069 --> 00:04:58.259
"See madness, as you know is like gravity.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.980
All it takes is a little push."

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:06.440
And sure, the Joker is eventually apprehended
and has his nihilistic philosophy thoroughly

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:10.259
disproven by the people of Gotham at the same
time — but everything else went off about

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.780
as well as he could have hoped.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.560
Christopher Nolan appears to have something
of a gift for letting the villains win.

00:05:15.569 --> 00:05:17.270
In this case, you've got Memento.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:21.840
The narrative follows Leonard Shelby, a man
who suffers from memory loss every five minutes.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.880
This is a recent affliction that has been
occurring ever since two men assaulted and

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:26.860
murdered his wife.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:30.520
After Shelby killed one of them, the other
knocked him on the head and escaped, leaving

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.080
him with his new mental handicap.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.331
Shelby is dead-set on hunting down the other
man responsible for his wife's death, but

00:05:36.331 --> 00:05:40.720
plagued with short-term memory loss, he is
forced to use tattoos and Polaroid cameras

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.729
in an elaborate system to remind himself of
what he discovers.

00:05:43.729 --> 00:05:48.280
The movie is filmed in both color and black-and-white
sequences, showing different angles of perception

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:52.889
and giving a sense of bizarre confusion that
helps the audience relate to the film's hero…

00:05:52.889 --> 00:05:54.420
except Shelby isn't the hero.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:58.780
As the movie concludes, we find that he has
been cyclically hunting down and taking "vengeance"

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:00.340
on innocent people for a year.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.780
Repressing this information, Shelby tampers
with his own photographic evidence, allowing

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:08.479
his condition to wash all guilt away within
the next few minutes and permitting him to

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.120
continue his villainous behavior.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:13.960
While Peter Jackson's film adaptation of J.R.R.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:17.270
Tolkien's awe-inspiring Lord of the Rings
trilogy has many happy moments during its

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:20.980
runtime, the ending of the first film, The
Fellowship of the Ring, isn't one of them.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:25.020
As the film reaches its crescendo, the Fellowship
has already gone through the devastating loss

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:29.520
of Gandalf, but things go from bad to worse
as the forces of Mordor close in on them.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:33.659
Boromir kicks things off by falling to the
lure of the ring and attempting to take it

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.480
from Frodo.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.440
Unsuccessful and repentant, Boromir and the
rest of the heroes turn their attention to

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:42.099
a sudden attack of Uruk-Hai soldiers sent
by Saruman to find the Ring.

00:06:42.099 --> 00:06:46.240
The attack splits the group up, with the villains
killing Boromir and successfully carrying

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:47.680
off the hobbits Merry and Pippin.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.700
Frodo, meanwhile, leaves with Sam across the
river, and the two begin to work their way

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:52.900
towards Mordor alone.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:57.100
All in all, this ending is about as chaotic
as it gets and doesn't lead to any one of

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.100
the protagonists actually getting their way.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:03.710
Though triumph lies ahead, the truth is that
Fellowship is a movie about the power of camaraderie

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:07.719
that nonetheless tears its characters away
from each other during its final moments.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.360
And that's about as bleak as it gets.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:13.979
Though it's outside the canon of the MCU and
doesn't have quite as catastrophic an ending

00:07:13.979 --> 00:07:18.479
as Infinity War, X-Men: First Class is another
Marvel movie that doesn't reward its heroes

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:19.320
with a happy ending.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:24.319
In this prequel to the original X-Men movies,
the storyline jumps back in time to the 1960s

00:07:24.319 --> 00:07:26.990
to explore the origin stories of its heroes
and villains.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:30.999
In particular, the film focuses on the development
of the relationship between Professor Charles

00:07:30.999 --> 00:07:35.169
Xavier and Erik Lehnsherr, which is the story
of a profound and meaningful friendship…

00:07:35.169 --> 00:07:36.620
right up until it isn't.

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:38.540
"We have it in us to be better men.”

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:39.780
“We already are.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.319
We are the next stage of human evolution you
said it yourself."

00:07:43.319 --> 00:07:47.480
While the movie itself brought a fresh spin
to a flagging franchise, its story ended on

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.960
a dark note, with the rise of an iconic Marvel
villain: Magneto.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:55.280
As the film enters its final act, the differences
between Xavier's and Lehnsherr's views on

00:07:55.289 --> 00:07:59.990
mutant activism come to a head, with Lehnsherr
dramatically parting ways with the critically-wounded

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:01.160
Xavier and his team.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:05.210
This sets him on his journey towards becoming
the franchise's most notable villain, and

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.580
begins a rivalry fated to go down in history.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:12.300
Like Valkyrie, Life is Beautiful is another
story that ends with the Nazis coming out

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:12.840
on top.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.820
This classic Italian film was directed and
co-written by the incredibly talented Roberto

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:22.930
Benigni, who also played the lead role alongside
Nicoletta Braschi, his wife of nearly thirty

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:23.420
years.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:28.120
The first half of the film is almost entirely
light and comedic as it follows Guido, a Jewish

00:08:28.139 --> 00:08:32.520
bookshop owner in Italy who shamelessly pursues
the love of his life with a little slapstick

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:34.380
clowning and a lot of Italian charm.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:38.840
But things take a drastic turn when the narrative
jumps forward several years to a Nazi-occupied

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:42.680
Italy, where Guido, his wife, and their son
are sent to a concentration camp.

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:47.460
Once in the camp, the bookshop owner uses
his incredibly resilient imagination to tirelessly

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:50.910
shield his son from the horrors around them,
convincing the young boy that they're on a

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.240
strange kind of holiday.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:56.740
Despite the subject matter, the movie does
actually build toward a happy ending… until,

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:01.000
in a gut-wrenching turn, Guido is gunned down
by Nazis just as the camp is liberated.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:05.230
And while Guido's son's innocence is preserved,
the loss of the film's lovable protagonist

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.720
is nonetheless a shocking note for the film
to end on.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:13.880
Just like the classic 1949 George Orwell novel
on which it's based, the movie 1984 is about

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.120
as depressing as it gets.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:20.030
From the infamous "Thought Police" to the
near-endless torture, brainwashing, and "doublethink,"

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:24.320
this movie pretty much established all the
classic tropes of futuristic, dystopian horror.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.380
The film is set in a world where the single,
united super-state of "Oceania" is run like

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:32.480
a well-oiled autocratic machine, in which
every move and thought of its inhabitants

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:36.140
is scrutinized for any deviation from government-approved
behavior.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:40.460
The story follows Winston Smith, a supposedly
loyal worker at the Ministry of Truth.

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:44.900
Smith "deviates" from the rules when he meets
Julia and begins to secretly pursue an affair

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.620
with the daring fellow thought-criminal.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:50.980
Of course, government forces prove much more
powerful than two people, and the end of the

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:54.790
movie shows the couple as they're caught and
put through a system of "rehabilitation,"

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:58.160
in which they are tortured and forced to face
their greatest fears in order to break their

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.340
rebellion and ensure their future cooperation
with the regime.

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:05.500
And that heart-breaking ending in the cafe,
in which Julia and Winston coldly admit they

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:09.960
betrayed each other, leaves no doubt whatsoever
that Big Brother has come out on top.

